{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question","id":1029084,"title":"Cross over / clash of wills question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-09T08:30:03-08:00","id":1029084,"title":"Cross over / clash of wills question.","content":"Help with scenario:<br /> A werewolf has used &quot;Knotted Path&quot; to trap a mage he's stalking in a large wooded park. The mage has Death 4, Life 3, Matter 4. Is there anything said mage could do that would directly oppose the effect / provoke a clash of wills with those Arcana, so he can leave the park? Or does he just need to prepare for a fight or hide? With Fate or Space or Spirit I can easily see it done, but I can't find it with the three arcana at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:57:00-08:00","id":1029095,"title":"","content":"Have a high Composure + Gnosis. It doesn't look like even destroying the wooded area would help, as it doesn't have to rely on the trees or whatever obstacles are there. I guess you could summon a ghost or something and have them escort you out. Providing the werewolf didn't get an Exceptional Success it does look like you could be led out, if they stick together or the werewolf doesn't just use it on the ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-09-2017, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:59:57-08:00","id":1029096,"title":"","content":"Patterning would be enough to open an existing Avernian Gate, which would probably prompt a Clash. Alternatively, you might be able to transform enough shadows/dead people/ghosts into a Gate.<br /> <br /> If shifting into Death-Twilight counts as 'escaping' (I could see arguments either way) then Ghost Gate may also prompt a CoW. Even if it doesn't, it makes the mage pretty safe from most standard werewolf abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-09-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:11:29-08:00","id":1029105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029095#post1029095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a high Composure + Gnosis. It doesn't look like even destroying the wooded area would help, as it doesn't have to rely on the trees or whatever obstacles are there. I guess you could summon a ghost or something and have them escort you out. Providing the werewolf didn't get an Exceptional Success it does look like you could be led out, if they stick together or the werewolf doesn't just use it on the ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage has failed to resist the effect, so composure won't help at this point.<br /> The ghost option is good, but it has already been established that there are no ghosts in this park. Thanks for the suggestion though - even if there were ghosts I would not have thought of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:16:41-08:00","id":1029107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029096#post1029096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Patterning would be enough to open an existing Avernian Gate, which would probably prompt a Clash. Alternatively, you might be able to transform enough shadows/dead people/ghosts into a Gate.<br /> <br /> If shifting into Death-Twilight counts as 'escaping' (I could see arguments either way) then Ghost Gate may also prompt a CoW. Even if it doesn't, it makes the mage pretty safe from most standard werewolf abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no existing gate, and the mage isn't skilled enough to create one (though if it was an option, I would think that, like using Space 3 to overlap to a different location, it wouldn't require a clash of wills - it would just involving leaving that location. I assumed only effects that let the mage walk out of the park would involve a clash of wills - such as using Fate 1 Serendipity to find the best path - not that just leaving isn't a better option).<br /> <br /> I don't think Ghost Gate counts as escaping, but it is the mage's go to effect to avoid being physically attached in cases wherein flight is not an option. Hopefully the wolf doesn't have any gifts that let him interact with death-twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:37:16-08:00","id":1029122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029107#post1029107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Ghost Gate counts as escaping, but it is the mage's go to effect to avoid being physically attached in cases wherein flight is not an option. Hopefully the wolf doesn't have any gifts that let him interact with death-twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barghest, great gift. Tell us how it turns out, if you would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:39:18-08:00","id":1029124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029107#post1029107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no existing gate, and the mage isn't skilled enough to create one</div> </div> </div> </div>Do keep in mind that Death 5 for making a Gate is only a requirement to create one ex-nihilo. Creating something under the purview of the Arcanum from other things under the purview of the Arcanum (eg, a Gate from ghosts/shadows/what have you) is explicitly possible via Creative Thaumaturgy at Patterning (Death 4)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:54:54-08:00","id":1029130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029124#post1029124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do keep in mind that Death 5 for making a Gate is only a requirement to create one ex-nihilo. Creating something under the purview of the Arcanum from other things under the purview of the Arcanum (eg, a Gate from ghosts/shadows/what have you) is explicitly possible via Creative Thaumaturgy at Patterning (Death 4)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I did not understand that apparently. There are definitely shadows to work with. Of course, now one has to decide if it is preferable to hide from a hostile werewolf in a wooded park, or traipse through the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:01:26-08:00","id":1029132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029130#post1029130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. I did not understand that apparently. There are definitely shadows to work with. Of course, now one has to decide if it is preferable to hide from a hostile werewolf in a wooded park, or traipse through the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hope it doesn't follow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:12:19-08:00","id":1029135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029124#post1029124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do keep in mind that Death 5 for making a Gate is only a requirement to create one ex-nihilo. Creating something under the purview of the Arcanum from other things under the purview of the Arcanum (eg, a Gate from ghosts/shadows/what have you) is explicitly possible via Creative Thaumaturgy at Patterning (Death 4)</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between &quot;make a new Avernian Gate&quot; and &quot;turn something else into an Avernian Gate&quot; is academic and Patterning very definitely cannot be that broad if the setting is to remain consistent \u2014 there's a reason there's no example spell for turning a pile of tass into a Hallow, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:25:15-08:00","id":1029141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029135#post1029135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between &quot;make a new Avernian Gate&quot; and &quot;turn something else into an Avernian Gate&quot; is academic and Patterning very definitely cannot be that broad if the setting is to remain consistent \u2014 there's a reason there's no example spell for turning a pile of tass into a Hallow, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's roughly as academic as the difference between creating a pillar of fire or transforming into one, ie not academic at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Patterning spells allow a mage to completely transform a<br /> target into something else that falls under the Arcanum\u2019s<br /> purview. A memory can be replaced wholesale (Mind),<br /> the mage can turn herself (or a target) into an animal<br /> (Life), or she can teleport by \u201crewriting\u201d her own location<br /> (Space). A spell that transforms the target into something<br /> that falls within the Purview of another Arcanum, like<br /> transforming into a living pillar of fire (Life and Forces),<br /> requires a mage to know the Practice of Patterning for the<br /> destination Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>Despite how inclined I might be to agree, Patterning has no such limitations described, and any imposed would need to be based on setting consistency / the desired atmosphere at the table, like pretty much everything with Creative Thaumaturgy. If incredibly broad transformations within the Arcana break versimillitude at your table, just buff up a ghost with Underworld Gate. <br /> There's nothing remotely special enough about Avernian Gates to restrict them to Death 5 only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:36:26-08:00","id":1029145,"title":"","content":"I thought about using the Underworld to escape as well, but the wording of Knotted Path suggests you might find yourself traveling back to the park.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:38:17-08:00","id":1029148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029141#post1029141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's roughly as academic as the difference between creating a pillar of fire or transforming into one, ie not academic at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gross Arcana don't cover entire separate realms of existence and their largely-uniformly-categorized denizens and the vast majority of Patterning spells are &quot;completely change something's classification in that Arcanum.&quot; You might as well claim that Weaving lets you treat any shadow <i>as though it were</i> an Avernian Gate because making it provide access to the Underworld doesn't necessitate turning it into something totally different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If incredibly broad transformations within the Arcana break versimillitude at your table, just buff up a ghost with Underworld Gate. </div> </div> </div>The Avernian Gate Manifestation is a key for opening existing Avernian Gates. It does not create a new instance of this phenomenon that only exists in locations with a specific Resonance. You'll notice that the Master-level spell <i>creates the Resonance</i> as part of its formation of an open Gate.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's nothing remotely special enough about Avernian Gates to restrict them to Death 5 only. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=873580#post873580\">The guy who developed the game disagrees.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:45:37-08:00","id":1029152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029148#post1029148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Avernian Gate Manifestation is a key for opening existing Avernian Gates. It does not create a new instance of this phenomenon that only exists in locations with a specific Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't what it says at all. You're reading the Description as if it were a prerequisite. It isn't. (Prerequisites have their own section, the description is what the condition is like after it's activated).<br /> <br /> The following section explains how to create it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Condition can be created by using the Avernian Gateway Manifestation Effect on an Open Condition. </div> </div> </div>You can create the Open Condition with Death 3, then Ghost with the appropriate Manifestation can use it, resulting in the Underworld Gate condition, which leads to: an open gateway to the Underworld. Shadow Gateway works the same way. Use the Manifestation on an Open Condition.<br /> <br /> If there were more specific requirements, they would be listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-09-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:56:19-08:00","id":1029158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029152#post1029152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can create the Open Condition with Death 3, then Ghost with the appropriate Manifestation can use it, resulting in the Underworld Gate condition, which leads to: an open gateway to the Underworld. Shadow Gateway works the same way. Use the Manifestation on an Open Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Open Condition is not universally applicable and does you no good if <i>there is no Gate present</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Ghost, angel or death-related spirit only \u2014 Requires Open Condition) By spending three Essence, the entity <b>opens a nearby gateway to the Underworld</b>, and applies the Underworld Gate Condition to the location. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doorways to the Underworld, also called Avernian gates, exist all over the world but are invisible to all but a handful of psychics. <b>The gateways are in Twilight, made of ghostly ephemera, and appear in places with the Resonant Condition tagged as \u201cDeath\u201d</b> \u2014 anywhere that people die in large numbers or that has a feel of Death about it can house a gate. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some supernatural beings with ties to death are also able to open Avernian Gateways. Even mortals can open a gate if one is present and they know the proper means. Mortals who <b>conduct rituals to first Open a Death-Resonant location that houses a gate</b> can unlock it, causing this Condition, but require the key to do so. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there were more specific requirements, they would be listed. </div> </div> </div>Wordcount is a thing and Mage does not treat the Underworld as a top priority. Arbitrary symmetry is a bad assumption to make for pretty much every game in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:02:23-08:00","id":1029159,"title":"","content":"None of those arguments are compelling, excepting this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>(Ghost, angel or death-related spirit only \u2014 Requires Open Condition) By spending three Essence, the entity </i><b>opens a nearby gateway to the Underworld</b><i>, and applies the Underworld Gate Condition to the location.</i> </div> </div> </div>This changes my perspective, with the clear implication that there must be a nearby gateway to open, especially contrasted with the phrasing for Shadow Gate:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Rank 3+ spirit or angel only \u2014 Requires Open Condition) By spending Essence<br /> equal to Gauntlet Strength, the entity opens a portal to the Shadow that it and<br /> other entities may use, applying the \u201cShadow Gate\u201d Condition to the location. The<br /> activation roll is penalized by the local Gauntlet Strength. </div> </div> </div>I was going off of the actual condition and how it says to cause it, not the chart summarizing all of them, which makes this more clear. Using an Avernian Gateway is probably out then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:22:59-08:00","id":1029170,"title":"","content":"Weaving can create Irises but you need a way of targeting the other side I guess. Co-location is an Iris by definition. Mastery can be a way of bypassing that maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:28:46-08:00","id":1029175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029170#post1029170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving can create Irises but you need a way of targeting the other side I guess. Co-location is an Iris by definition. Mastery can be a way of bypassing that maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Co-Location is a use of the Arcanum most directly concerned with Irises as a general phenomenon to connect two places not divided by a fairly opaque transdimensional interface \u2014 a normal Space Iris is a shortcut, not a threshold between worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T12:07:13-08:00","id":1029191,"title":"","content":"While I'm agreeing that Death only at Mastery could force a way to Underworld the Space suffers no such limitations. All you need is a pinch o Sympathy and Sympathy Yantra to superimpose two places at 3rd dot, be it Material, Shadow or Underworld - no need for anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T12:12:15-08:00","id":1029193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question#post1029084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage has Death 4, Life 3, Matter 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space ain't gonna help in this case.<br /> <br /> Someone else mentioned jumping into Twilight. That seems like the safest bet as long as one of the werewolves don't have that power that allows them to interact with entities in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T12:24:51-08:00","id":1029199,"title":"","content":"Back to topic. Yea, space won't help. Life can Veil you from all life, so go to Twilight, Veil yourself and wait. You could maybe hide Twilight as well? Reinforce it?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or force an animal to flee and follow it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-09-2017, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:04:44-08:00","id":1029216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029199#post1029199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to topic. Yea, space won't help. Life can Veil you from all life, so go to Twilight, Veil yourself and wait. You could maybe hide Twilight as well? Reinforce it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately: Lure and Repel. Life 3 should give you enough Reach to get Instant Casting and Advanced Duration, and from there you can drop two dice on Area Scale and add Potency dependent upon the werewolf's Resolve. Werewolves lose a fairly large number of their universal options for dealing with prey when they can't get within melee range.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the much more prosaic option of faking your death, but without the larger context it's difficult to say how inadvisable that course of action might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:33:23-08:00","id":1029267,"title":"","content":"Shadow Flesh seems like another pretty safe bet; the spell description says the Mage is &quot;immune to attacks or damage, but not Supernal magic&quot; which basically leaves the Werewolf high and dry (though Gifts may still work, depending on their effect.<br /> <br /> Plus, if the Mage becomes a two-dimensional shadow, they can hide in a 1mm wide crevasse - which they can create themselves with another Death or Matter spell. Since the shadow presumably doesn't generate a smell or taste, has no physical effect on the world and makes no sound, I don't think even Werewolf senses will be able to pick it up - and you can always shape the shadows around you to ensure the sight aspect is covered.<br /> <br /> At that point, you could probably turn the tables and ambush the hunter by, say, hitting them with Aggravated damage spells or converting the air around them into chlorine gas or whatnot. Unless the Werewolf has some nice spirits on-side or a bunch of magic-like gifts, I'd say the Mage should be fine.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you don't use Shadow Flesh without Life 4, you can basically still hide - though much less effectively - by shaping your way into something like a cliff-face and then just convert rock into air as needed. The Werewolf will probably find you, but may not be able to do much, since if they try to get in you can shape a path away from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","user":"Eggs Maledict","date":".  Shadow Flesh weirdness 01-09-2017, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T15:50:34-08:00","id":1029303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029216#post1029216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately: Lure and Repel. Life 3 should give you enough Reach to get Instant Casting and Advanced Duration, and from there you can drop two dice on Area Scale and add Potency dependent upon the werewolf's Resolve. Werewolves lose a fairly large number of their universal options for dealing with prey when they can't get within melee range.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the much more prosaic option of faking your death, but without the larger context it's difficult to say how inadvisable that course of action might beWow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of using something like that on the werewolf - keeping him at a distance and then fighting didn't really occur (the bastards are so tough) but it is an idea if I can't hide or if he can attack in twilight.<br /> <br /> However, you and Moinen together did give me a workable idea. Repel on an animal while perhaps using instinct control to keep him from moving too fast, then just follow the squirrel / feral dog / cat / crow out of the park. It would at least give me a chance to clash wills and avoid the confrontation that I don't want (my character isn't much of a fighter). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 01-09-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T15:53:09-08:00","id":1029304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eggs Maledict</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029267#post1029267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Flesh seems like another pretty safe bet; the spell description says the Mage is &quot;immune to attacks or damage, but not Supernal magic&quot; which basically leaves the Werewolf high and dry (though Gifts may still work, depending on their effect.<br /> <br /> Plus, if the Mage becomes a two-dimensional shadow, they can hide in a 1mm wide crevasse - which they can create themselves with another Death or Matter spell. Since the shadow presumably doesn't generate a smell or taste, has no physical effect on the world and makes no sound, I don't think even Werewolf senses will be able to pick it up - and you can always shape the shadows around you to ensure the sight aspect is covered.<br /> <br /> At that point, you could probably turn the tables and ambush the hunter by, say, hitting them with Aggravated damage spells or converting the air around them into chlorine gas or whatnot. Unless the Werewolf has some nice spirits on-side or a bunch of magic-like gifts, I'd say the Mage should be fine.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you don't use Shadow Flesh without Life 4, you can basically still hide - though much less effectively - by shaping your way into something like a cliff-face and then just convert rock into air as needed. The Werewolf will probably find you, but may not be able to do much, since if they try to get in you can shape a path away from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do house rule that Life 4 is needed for Shadow Flesh. There are no rocks / cliffs in the park. I guess I could try to find a dead tree, get inside, then turn it to stone, using Matter to cover my spore ...<br /> <br /> Ideas abound even if I can't get out of the park. Thanks everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:09:43-08:00","id":1029316,"title":"","content":"Man now I want to play werewolf more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:36:15-08:00","id":1029330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029304#post1029304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We do house rule that Life 4 is needed for Shadow Flesh. There are no rocks / cliffs in the park. I guess I could try to find a dead tree, get inside, then turn it to stone, using Matter to cover my spore ...<br /> <br /> Ideas abound even if I can't get out of the park. Thanks everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even just into the ground probably, especially if you also shift into Twilight. I'd suggest spreading spoor everywhere rather than trying to hide it, given the bonuses Uratha get.<br /> <br /> Although...if you DID hide in a tree and turn it to, say, titanium (then magically harden it further), you could use Golem to animate it and mecha-battle the KaijUratha!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:56:18-08:00","id":1029344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eggs Maledict</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029330#post1029330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Although...if you DID hide in a tree and turn it to, say, titanium (then magically harden it further), you could use Golem to animate it and mecha-battle the KaijUratha!</div> </div> </div> </div>That is beautifull \ud83d\ude02","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:19:24-08:00","id":1029360,"title":"","content":"&quot;No matter what they do, the prey cannot escape the area that they are in for the Facet's duration.&quot; The mage can summon some critter and follow it all day - it's not going to lead you out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:25:44-08:00","id":1029362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029360#post1029360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No matter what they do, the prey cannot escape the area that they are in for the Facet's duration.&quot; The mage can summon some critter and follow it all day - it's not going to lead you out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves be dangerous, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:30:10-08:00","id":1029367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question#post1029084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Help with scenario:<br /> A werewolf has used &quot;Knotted Path&quot; to trap a mage he's stalking in a large wooded park. The mage has Death 4, Life 3, Matter 4. Is there anything said mage could do that would directly oppose the effect / provoke a clash of wills with those Arcana, so he can leave the park? Or does he just need to prepare for a fight or hide? With Fate or Space or Spirit I can easily see it done, but I can't find it with the three arcana at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pray to whatever gods he claims he can one shot a werewolf and that for some reason the pack isn't right behind him, odds are.<br /> <br /> Or he could try negotiating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T17:34:14-08:00","id":1029372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029360#post1029360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No matter what they do, the prey cannot escape the area that they are in for the Facet's duration.&quot; The mage can summon some critter and follow it all day - it's not going to lead you out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you can't find a power to try a Clash of Wills, it's basically hide or fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T19:41:20-08:00","id":1029434,"title":"","content":"A day long duration on Knotted Path, too. So it would be a long wait. I'm doubtful it's about a hunt, just based on what little we know.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining it's more a 'don't run away, I need to talk to you.' My werewolves always pulled them off in ways that seem more like he's trying to kill them. Very impulsive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:31:24-08:00","id":1029676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029084-cross-over-clash-of-wills-question?p=1029316#post1029316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man now I want to play werewolf more.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Hunter in Darkness pack literally dealt with Pure by driving them to mass Kuruth, then using Knotted Paths and, after their rage assuming most didn't tear each other apart, simply murdered them while they passed out post rage.<br /> <br /> They avoided our territory like the plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T12:29:17-08:00","id":1029702,"title":"","content":"Since escape seems unlikely, time to turn the place into a death-trap. As an Adept of Matter (and a Moros, unless I'm mistaken), you can reshape the surrounding into all kinds of &quot;fun&quot;.<br /> <br /> Check out the common &quot;101 ways to kill you with Arcanum X at 3 dots or less&quot; threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}